{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/453202-on-the-nature-of-the-werewolf-and-its-effect-on-the-game","id":453202,"title":"On the nature of the werewolf and its effect on the game.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-22T14:54:13-07:00","id":453202,"title":"On the nature of the werewolf and its effect on the game.","content":"Werewolf has a great difference with the rest of the nwod lines in that its characters are objective driven. The wolf must hunt,and because of that werewolfs games are more likely to be similar to each other than games in the other nwod lines.<br /> <br /> It could end up being a game of hunt after hunt, with little diferences throught the campaign. I feel that every game would be about identifying the dangers and prey in the territory and erradicating it. Sure you can add aditional ideas in the periphery, but two of the three themes in the game explicitly remark on this aspect of the game. The wolf must hunt and the inherent duty (the duty of hunting).<br /> <br /> Im trying to set up a werewolf game with my group, but everything i can thing about is &quot;what are the characters going to hunt?&quot;<br /> <br /> I know I might be oversimplifying things. Im doing it for the sake of argument and i genuinely want to know what else is there in werewolf the forsaken.<br /> <br /> Thinking about this, I have decided tht the game should focus on characterization a lot, emphazsing the duality of the characters and the experience of being a werewolf and using the hunt and the events in the game as a vehicule for this experience.<br /> <br /> So, what do you guys think? Is werewolf limited by its rich setting and explicit objectives for the characters? Is this how its suppose to be and if it is, is it a good thing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2245-quimeradc","name":"Quimeradc","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T14:58:51-07:00","id":453221,"title":"","content":"I think you're placing so much emphasis on the hunt you're overlooking the fact that characters are people and have their own wants and needs. You should look at the backgrounds of your characters, their aspirations, and build from there, instead of just giving them things to hunt.<br /> <br /> Also, Mages are driven by looking into mysteries, Prometheans by becoming human, Mummies by finding relics, each of the Demon factions has their own special aspiration for things they're looking for. And Hunter the Vigil of course is about hunting monsters. But all the games manage to have a lot more depth than those few words can ascribe to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 03-22-2015, 06:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T15:10:33-07:00","id":453234,"title":"","content":"You're looking at it backwards. Yes, werewolves are a bit obsessed with hunting, but what they will end up doing is framing everything they do in terms of a hunt. Need to fight a spirit? Hunt! Construction threatening a locus? Hunt! Researching a town's history? Hunt! Buying a new car? Hunt!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T17:54:56-07:00","id":453460,"title":"","content":"The other half of things, and the reason that the new book was going to be called The Idigam Chronicles before it was just called Second Edition, is that as much as the main characters want to be hunting, there are things out there that are hunting them, things that are well beyond their ability to handle.<br /> Sure you could have hunt after hunt, you could put prey after prey in front of your characters for them to rip apart week after week (or night after night or month after month depending on how often you meet), or you could give them a big, multi-faceted problem. With that, they can spend sessions hunting down tiny facets of a solution that could, just maybe, build to a resolution to the otherwise insurmountable issue before them. Elfive is totally right that anything the characters do could be a hunt (even a Sacred Hunt if they so choose), but you could sculpt it a bit so that all those little hunts lead somewhere.<br /> Nofather also has a great point about what to sprinkle your game with along the way. Without connection to the story, even facing a big threat can be meaningless. Find out who the characters are and run with the things they care about. Threaten the stuff they care about and give them opportunities to fulfil their aspirations along the way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T23:07:00-07:00","id":453884,"title":"","content":"Looking for story ideas? <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/11952-1001-werewolf-story-hooks\">Try my story hooks thread. </a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}